{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TauAllOrdersBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TauAllOrdersBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tau_h2_anchor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tau_h2_anchor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tau_h2_anchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tau_h2_anchor","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L155-L159","doc":"The h² anchor value of the kernel's leading coefficient, fixed by\nthe proved algebraic Euler characteristic and the Markov-trace h²\ncoefficient. This number is determined regardless of which\nhypothesis holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tau_order_mixing_naive_hyp1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tau_order_mixing_naive_hyp1","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L131-L139","doc":"The **naive hypothesis (1)** alone (retained for the record) — NOT a\ndichotomy/disjunction, just the existence of an arbitrary\nlower-triangular order-mixing map (Copilot review #1858: the body is\n`Nonempty (TauOrderMixingMap α κ)`, a single existence claim, so the\nname now reflects that). For the probed Borromean sequences this is\ntrivially inhabited (#1837), which is precisely why it is superseded\nby the banded dichotomy `tau_all_orders_bridge`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tau_all_orders_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tau_all_orders_bridge","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L114-L129","doc":"**Conjecture (τ at all orders — dichotomy, refined per #1837).**\nFor the Borromean algebraic/Markov coefficient sequences `α`, `κ`,\none of the two hypotheses holds: the fibre functor τ is a\nfinite-support convolution kernel (`TauBandedKernelMap`), or no such\nkernel exists and the two sides measure distinct invariants\n(`TauDistinctInvariants`).\n\nThis is the **non-trivial** form. The earlier\n`tau_order_mixing_naive_hyp1` below (arbitrary lower-triangular `T`)\nis excluded-middle-vacuous because hypothesis (1) is always\ninhabited there (#1837); the banded-kernel constraint is what makes\nthe disjunction informative. Neither class currently has an instance\nfor the categorical sequences — the honest reflection of the open\nstatus. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:tau-all-orders-bridge","label":"conj:tau-all-orders-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants.noKernelAtAllOrders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants.noKernelAtAllOrders","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L108-L108","doc":"For every finitely-supported kernel `f` (vanishing beyond some\nband `N`), the convolution bridge fails at some order `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauDistinctInvariants","kind":"class","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L93-L112","doc":"Hypothesis (2) of `conj:tau-all-orders-bridge`, parameterised by the\nsame fixed sequences `α`, `κ`: no finite-support convolution kernel\nsatisfies the bridge at all orders, so the algebraic and Markov-trace\nsides measure genuinely different categorical invariants of the\nBorromean braid that share only the h² value.\n\nQuantifier order (Gemini + Copilot review #1830): for the FIXED\n`α`, `κ`, every candidate finitely-supported kernel `f` fails the\nconvolution bridge at some order `k`. Stated against the *banded*\nkernel (not an arbitrary lower-triangular `T`) so that it is the\ngenuine negation of the refined hypothesis (1) — the arbitrary-`T`\nnegation would be vacuously false (#1837). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The bridge as a convolution with the SAME kernel at every order:\n`κ_k = Σ_{j ≤ k} kernel(k − j) · α_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.leadingNonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.leadingNonzero","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The leading (diagonal) coefficient `T_{k,k} = kernel 0` is\nnon-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.finiteSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.finiteSupport","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Finite support — the defining restriction that makes the map a\nsingle operator with finitely many parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.bandWidth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.bandWidth","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The band half-width: the kernel vanishes beyond `bandWidth`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.kernel","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The convolution kernel: `T_{k,j} = kernel (k − j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauBandedKernelMap","kind":"class","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L58-L91","doc":"Hypothesis (1) of `conj:tau-all-orders-bridge`, **refined\n(non-trivial) form** — the genuine open content per #1837.\n\nA fibre-functor realisation of τ does not supply an arbitrary\nlower-triangular `T` (which is vacuously available, see the caveat\non `TauOrderMixingMap`); it supplies a SINGLE convolution operator\nwith **finitely many** degrees of freedom — a kernel `f` of bounded\nsupport, with `T_{k,j} = f(k − j)`. The bridge then reads\n`κ = f ⋆ α` and must hold at EVERY order `k` with the *same* `f`,\nso a band of width `bandWidth + 1` real unknowns faces infinitely\nmany equations. That is the over-determined, non-vacuous constraint:\n`Nonempty (TauBandedKernelMap α κ)` is a substantive claim about the\ncategorical sequences, not an artefact of per-row freedom.\n\n(Structurally `f(0)` is the diagonal — `T_{k,k} = f(0)` — pinned at\n`h²` to `f(0) = κ₂/α₂ = -1/64`; the disproof in\n`phi0_normalization_disproof.py` shows no *constant* kernel\n`f = (f(0), 0, 0, …)` works past `h²`, so the open question is\nwhether a *wider* finite band closes the bridge.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.bridgeAtOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.bridgeAtOrder","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The bridge for the fixed sequences:\nκ_{2k} = Σ_{j ≤ k} T_{k,j} · α_{2j} for every k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.diagonalNonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.diagonalNonzero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Diagonal entries are non-zero (T is invertible on each truncation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.lowerTriangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.lowerTriangular","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Lower triangular: zero above the diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.tauCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.tauCoeff","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L48-L48","doc":"T_{k,j} for j ≤ k, the (k,j)-entry of the order-mixing map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TauOrderMixingMap","kind":"class","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tau-all-orders-bridge.lean#L16-L56","doc":"Hypothesis (1) of `conj:tau-all-orders-bridge`, **naive form**,\nparameterised by the FIXED algebraic coefficient sequence `α` (the\nh^{2k}-curvature traces of the Q₈ crossed module along the Borromean\nbraid) and the FIXED Markov-trace sequence `κ` (the h^{2k}\ncoefficients of the Jones polynomial of the same braid). Index\n`k : ℕ` stands for the even order 2k.\n\nThe fibre functor τ is realised by a lower-triangular linear map on\nthe h-graded expansion taking `α` to `κ`. Both `α` and `κ` are class\nparameters — NOT universally quantified inside the bridge field —\nthus the class is satisfiable for the specific categorical sequences\n(Gemini + Copilot review #1830: a single `tauCoeff` cannot satisfy\nthe bridge for *all* sequences, e.g. α = 0, κ = 1).\n\n**CAVEAT (#1837 — trivially inhabited *for the probed dataset*).**\nThe h⁶ empirical probe (`tau_all_orders_h6_empirical.py`) showed that\nat a fixed substrate `q₀` both `α` and `κ` are constant sequences,\nand `tauCoeff` has *independent free entries per row*, so every row\n`κ k = Σ_{j ≤ k} tauCoeff k j · α j` is a one-equation /\n`k`-unknowns underdetermined system solved on its own — *provided\neach such row has at least one nonzero `α j`, `j ≤ k`*, which holds\nfor the Borromean sequences (`α₂ = -12`, `α₄ = -6` nonzero). Under\nthat condition `Nonempty (TauOrderMixingMap α κ)` is trivially\ninhabited and does NOT capture the open question. (Copilot review\n#1858: for *arbitrary* fixed `α, κ` the class can be uninhabited —\ne.g. `α j = 0` for all `j ≤ k` but `κ k ≠ 0` makes row `k`\nunsatisfiable — so this is a statement about the specific\ncategorical dataset, not all sequences.) The genuine refinement is\n`TauBandedKernelMap` below, which forces a SINGLE finite-support\nconvolution kernel across all orders. ","signatureChunk":0}]}